# Cline Rules for CesiumJS WebGPU Project — SUPERSEDED POINTER

**This file is no longer a rules authority. The rules live in `CLAUDE.md` at the
repository root.**

## Where the rules are now

`CLAUDE.md` (repository root) is the tracked rules authority. It was made a
tracked file in the same batch that demoted this one, so a fresh clone now
receives the live rules rather than only this frozen copy.

- **Cline users:** `CLAUDE.md` is plain markdown in the same directory. Read it
  in place of this file. If your setup can only auto-load `.clinerules`, load
  `CLAUDE.md` manually at the start of a session — do not work from this file.
- **Precedence** between the tracked governance documents is set by
  `migration_doc/EXECUTOR_LANE_CHARTER_2026-08-14.md` §0.4, not here.
- **Campaign status** is `migration_doc/CAMPAIGN_STATE.md` (R-2026-09-02-14).
- **Routing** (which tracked document answers each governed question) is the
  "Rules Files and Routing" section of `CLAUDE.md`; `AGENTS.md` (Codex) and
  `GEMINI.md` (Antigravity) are pointers to `CLAUDE.md` too (R-2026-10-30-M2).

## On-demand rule files

`CLAUDE.md` keeps its task-specific rules in skill files that Claude Code loads on demand. They bind
you as fully as `CLAUDE.md` does: read the matching file before the work it covers (`CLAUDE.md`,
"On-demand Skills", says when).

- [`.claude/skills/wgsl-shader-pipeline/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/wgsl-shader-pipeline/SKILL.md) — WGSL shader defines, the `//>>ifdef` preprocessor, the module cache, adding a define bit, pipeline-key aliasing.
- [`.claude/skills/build-and-variants/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/build-and-variants/SKILL.md) — build and test commands, bundle variants, compat exemptions, smoke test, visual regression, Playwright / Edge.
- [`.claude/skills/logging-pragmas/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/logging-pragmas/SKILL.md) — engine logs: what takes a debug pragma, what stays permanent, sentinels for new subsystems.
- [`.claude/skills/upstream-sync/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/upstream-sync/SKILL.md) — merging CesiumGS `upstream/main` into the fork.
- [`.claude/skills/wasm-strategy/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/wasm-strategy/SKILL.md) — WASM bridges, fallbacks, loading, memory, toolchains, threading.
- [`.claude/skills/debug-console/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/debug-console/SKILL.md) — `CesiumDebug` console commands; recording a fixed bug.
- [`.claude/skills/engine-code-standards/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/engine-code-standards/SKILL.md) — engine code: architecture patterns, RTE precision, file placement, file size, tech stack, ES6, comments and JSDoc.
- [`.claude/skills/probe-kit/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/probe-kit/SKILL.md) — the probe kit (kit-first order, guide sync) and the probe-first workflow for verifying a rendering fix.
- [`.claude/skills/seat-duties/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/seat-duties/SKILL.md) — the seat's duties (the landing route, quiet-hours enforcement, the evidence sweep); its "Branch transparency" binds you whenever `CLAUDE.md` "Branch Transparency" says, the rest only if you hold the seat. If the maintainer hands you the seat, read all of it: the seat's duties then apply to you, and this file's clone-only rules give way to them.
- [`.claude/skills/worker-rules/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/worker-rules/SKILL.md) — the worker-rules digest a lead reads before it briefs, a reviewer before it reviews, and any other lane agent before its first action.

Its history as the fork's former rules file, and what happened to each of its rules: `migration_doc/RULES_FILE_NOTES.md` section 6.
